<figure id="S4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T4.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">TABLE IV</span>: </span><span id="S4.T4.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Syntax highlighting accuracy results for invalid language derivations (code snippets)
across different programming languages, coverage tasks, and models. This table
compares multi-language (<em id="S4.T4.7.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ML<span id="S4.T4.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">⁢</span></em>) models (RQ2) with state-of-the-art single-language
(<em id="S4.T4.7.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">SL<span id="S4.T4.7.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">⁢</span></em>) models (RQ1) and their variants using token normalization <em id="S4.T4.7.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">+TN</em>, reporting
accuracy values averaged over three-fold cross-validation.
</span></figcaption>
